From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Jenkins <lukejenkins@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] mhi_init: declare "ADB" channel (36/37) in chan_cfg[]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Quectel out-of-tree pcie_mhi v1.3.6 defines MHI_CLIENT_ADB_FB_OUT
(36) and MHI_CLIENT_ADB_FB_IN (37) in core/mhi.h, but those constants
are not referenced anywhere in chan_cfg[]. Without an entry in
chan_cfg[], the MHI core never assigns chan_name = "ADB" to any
mhi_dev, so the matching UCI table entry that ships in patch 0002
would never fire and /dev/mhi_ADB would never appear.

This first half of the two-patch series adds the missing declaration
so the MHI core can name and bring up channels 36/37 when the modem
firmware advertises them. Whether the firmware actually advertises
those channels — and whether they carry runtime adbd traffic vs only
fastboot-mode ADB — is the empirical question; this patch makes the
experiment possible.

Validated on Quectel RM520N-GL-AP (firmware R01A07_11.204.11.204) and
Foxconn T99W640 / Dell DW5934e (SDX72). Not submitted upstream
(Quectel does not accept community patches to this OOT driver).

Reference: README.md (ADB-over-MHI findings).
Signed-off-by: Luke Jenkins <lukejenkins@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 core/mhi_init.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/core/mhi_init.c	2026-04-17 18:37:47.115446508 +0000
+++ b/core/mhi_init.c	2026-04-17 18:37:42.618440806 +0000
@@ -1810,6 +1810,9 @@
 //"Qualcomm EDL "
 	{"EDL", MHI_CLIENT_EDL_OUT, NUM_MHI_CHAN_RING_ELEMENTS},
 	{"EDL", MHI_CLIENT_EDL_IN, NUM_MHI_CHAN_RING_ELEMENTS},
+//"Qualcomm PCIe ADB (channels 36/37, MHI_CLIENT_ADB_FB_*)"
+	{"ADB", MHI_CLIENT_ADB_FB_OUT, NUM_MHI_CHAN_RING_ELEMENTS},
+	{"ADB", MHI_CLIENT_ADB_FB_IN, NUM_MHI_CHAN_RING_ELEMENTS},
 #ifdef ENABLE_IP_SW0
 //"Qualcomm PCIe LOCAL Adapter"
 	{"IP_SW0", MHI_CLIENT_IP_SW_0_OUT, NUM_MHI_SW_IP_RING_ELEMENTS},
